/haus_of_altr","https://www.instagram.com/hausofaltr/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/231707/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"231707","image":"https://i.discogs.com/gpLHWAVwih2LiXC8UUWYCsH5YMA9ECWOdicds4FWF4A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTIzMTcw/Ny0xMjk3ODQ3MTk2/LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/BOJcpxwp3xts5GX8Zdaqa1o1sMJFoZSYY4jjgeOC0IU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTIzMTcw/Ny0xMjk3ODQ3MTk2/LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"[b]Diskotopia[/b] is a Tokyo-based record label run by [a=A Taut Line] (Matt Lyne) and [a=BD1982] (Brian Durr) since 2011. The project started in 2005 as a DJ and visual collective, when British and American expats Matt and Brian started organizing club events in Osaka and Tokyo with a local resident DJ Am Rhein. Five years later, Diskotopia founders decided to expand their activities and established a record label. A Taut Line shares an art-direction responsibility at the label with a fellow design studio [l=Neithercorp].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:231707","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":[{"id":519129,"name":"A Kind Of Presence"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/231707-Diskotopia","type":"label","urls":["http://diskotopia.com","https://diskotopia.bandcamp.com","https://soundcloud.com/diskotopia","https://www.mixcloud.com/diskotopia","https://www.facebook.com/diskotopia","https://twitter.com/diskotopia"]}},"/api/discogs/label/32866/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"32866","image":"https://i.discogs.com/ngY18pydpLMglROu57G_CRX0OjduuYMeYCxIsTunv5A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:120/w:300/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMyODY2/LTEyMjc4MTMyODEu/anBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/9TDEVAmoioq4ZwVmvumLkdy4Mc0hxP-eQ5YonEs_21c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMyODY2/LTEyMjc4MTMyODEu/anBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Warner Strategic Marketing is responsible for the development and promotion of Warner's back catalogue including reissues, remasters, special editions, tracks never previously released, rarities and collectors' editions. See also [l=WSM] when a different logo is used.\r\nIn 2006 this responsibility was passed to [l33244] in an effort to improve Warner's flagging market share of the back catalogue and compilation market. \r\nFrom this point Warner Strategic Marketing handled distribution and the promotion Rhino Records' releases. (Issues may carry Label Code: LC 03708 or LC 02828).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:32866","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":2345,"name":"Warner Music Group"},"sublabels":[{"id":230096,"name":"Atlantic Jazz Masters"},{"id":231230,"name":"Atlantic Masters"},{"id":478732,"name":"Elektra Jazz Masters"},{"id":231232,"name":"Elektra Masters"},{"id":792809,"name":"Expanded & Remastered"},{"id":465745,"name":"Warner Bros. Jazz Masters"},{"id":146539,"name":"Warner Bros. Masters"},{"id":590910,"name":"Warner Strategic Marketing Brasil"},{"id":175153,"name":"Warner Strategic Marketing Canada"},{"id":289681,"name":"Warner Strategic Marketing Germany"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/32866-Warner-Strategic-Marketing","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/36012/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"36012","image":"https://i.discogs.com/4vPLD4FPo25OdW5Nchpk-1WlxM3B-D4MQYcNmAmFnJk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:320/w:305/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTM2MDEy/LTE2NDU2NTE1NzUt/ODgzNi5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/NVESSojLhGU2JaLkyfXD483fP18jOhn_SuTh-CMW7Nc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTM2MDEy/LTE2NDU2NTE1NzUt/ODgzNi5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"US label. The Ode label was founded by [a=Lou Adler] in 1967, soon after he had sold his successful [l=Dunhill] label to [l=ABC Records]. Ode was distributed by [l=Columbia]/[l=CBS] from 1967 to 1969, and [l904] from 1970 to 1976. (For 1970 only, to highlight the change of distribution and re-launch the label, the circular Ode logo had a '7' prepended, making it appear as 'Ode 70.' The logo was reverted in 1971.) In 1977, Adler put the Ode catalog up for sale so he could focus on motion pictures. In August, the catalog was acquired by Epic, with Adler becoming a consultant. Records would carry the combined Epic / Ode branding. In the US, CBS took over shortly afterwards with records returning to the 'Ode' branding.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, Adler had started [l=Ode Sounds & Visuals] for his motion picture efforts. By the end of the 1970s, the two labels were largely dormant.\r\n\r\nIn 1989, Adler reactivated the [l=Ode Sounds And Visuals] label. \r\nThe CBS-distributed Ode albums (namely the [a=Carole King] and [a=Tom Scott] material) is now owned by [l=Sony Music Entertainment] while the [a272936] albums went with the stoner comedy duo to [l=Warner Bros. Records]. The remainder of the Ode catalog (excluding the [i]Rocky Horror[/i] recordings, which Adler still owns) now rests with [l=Interscope Records] and [l=UMe].\r\n\r\nSee [l=Ode (8)] for company credits that mention just Ode or Ode, USA. Related publisher credits are [l2444104] & [l264237].\r\n\r\nLabel Code: [b]LC 1193 / 01193[/b]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:36012","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":107399,"name":"Ode Records Inc."},"sublabels":[{"id":222627,"name":"Ode 2 Kids"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/36012-Ode-Records-2","type":"label","urls":["https://www.onamrecords.com/labels/ode-records","https://www.bsnpubs.com/aandm/ode.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode_Records","https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Record-World/70s/70/RW-1970-05-02.pdf","https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Record-World/70s/70/RW-1970-03-28.pdf","https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Billboard/70s/1970/BB-1970-03-28.pdf","https://www.worldradiohistory.com/Archive-All-Music/Billboard/